 [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/FBL'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Football at the 1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "28 August –  5 September 1920"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/243"} "Olympisch Stadion, Antwerpen"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/256"} "Jules Ottenstadion, Gent"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/257"} "Stade du Parc Duden, Saint-Gilles"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/259"} "Stadion Broodstraat, Antwerpen"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The 1920 Olympic tournament was the first time that the early matches were spread around the host nation, rather than centered in the host city. This was the forerunner of the modern style, which is still used at the Olympics and the FIFA World Cup. Most of the matches were held in Antwerpen, using two different stadia, but some early round matches were also held in Ghent and Saint-Gilles, a municipality of Bruxelles. From the quarter-finals onward, and including the second- and third-place matches, most of the matches were played in the " [:a {:href "/venues/243"} "Beerschot Stadium"] ", the main Olympic Stadium."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Stade de AA La Gantoise was built in 1919-20 for the Olympics, and was later renamed the " [:a {:href "/venues/256"} "Jules Ottenstadion"] ". It was in use until 2013, when it was demolished, and KAA Ghent (Koninklijke Atletiek Associatie Ghent / Royal Athletic Association Ghent) moved to Arteveldestadion. " [:a {:href "/venues/257"} "Stade de Union St. Gilloise"] " was opened in 1919, and is still in existence (as of 2024) in Duden Park, in Bruxelles, now called the Stade Joseph Marien. The Antwerpen sites were the " [:a {:href "/venues/259"} "Stade Royal Antwerp Football Club"] ", which hosted the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/614"} "Royal Antwerp Football Club"] " from 1908-23, and the Beerschot Stadium, the main Olympic Stadium for the Antwerpen Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There were some controversy about who could compete in 1920 Olympic football. Germany and Hungary, top football nations, were excluded from the Olympics entirely because of their recent role in World War I. Great Britain almost did not compete.  In early 1919, England, Ireland, Scotland, and Wales withdrew from " [:a {:href "/organizations/7"} "FIFA"] " and formed their own federation, the Federation of National Football Associations.  Surprisingly, the United States protested Britain’s presence in the 1920 football tournament, since Great Britain was no longer a FIFA member.  Belgium and France supported this motion, but Great Britain was allowed to compete.  Among the original 15 entries, Switzerland withdrew for financial reasons, leaving 14 nations in the field."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The biggest controversy of the 1920 football tournament took place in the final, between Belgium and Czechoslovakia. When a foul was called against a Czechoslovak player at the 39-minute mark, Czechoslovakia protested and eventually left the field, withdrawing in anger over the officiating. They would not return to the field and Belgium was declared the Olympic champion by default."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/33556"} "Football, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 August –  5 September 1920"] "\n" [:td {} "190"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n190 (190/0)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n14 (14/0)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n\n" [:h2 {} "Medals"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {:class "top"} [:a {:href "/results/33556"} "Football, Men"]] "\n" [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} "Belgium"] [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] "\n" [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} "Spain"] [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]] "\n" [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} "Netherlands"]